## CI/CD

**CI** (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`) — quality + security (Gitleaks + Trivy) on every push. No secrets required.

**Deploy** (`.github/workflows/deploy.yml`) — runs **only after CI passes**:

```text
Push → CI (lint, test, security scan) → pass? → Deploy to AWS
                                      → fail?  → no deploy
```

| After CI success on | GitHub environment | SST stage |
|---------------------|-------------------|-----------|
| `develop` (default branch) | `dev` | `dev` |
| `main` (create when ready for staging) | `staging` | `staging` |
| Manual dispatch → production | `production` | `production` |

Manual deploy (dev/staging/production) is also available from **Actions → Deploy → Run workflow** when needed.

### Branch strategy

New repositories are created on **`develop`** (not `main`). Push to `develop` → CI → dev deploy.

When ready for staging:

```sh
git checkout develop
git checkout -b main
git push -u origin main
```

Optionally set `main` as the default branch in GitHub repo settings for staging-focused workflows.

### One-time AWS + GitHub setup

1. Deploy IAM roles (once per org):

```sh
cd platform-infra
npm install
cp .env.example .env   # GITHUB_ORG=Randipa
export $(grep -v '^#' .env | xargs)
npm run deploy:platform
```

2. In the GitHub repo → **Settings** → **Environments**, create `dev`, `staging`, `production`.

3. Add secret `AWS_ROLE_ARN` in each environment:

| Environment | Role (from platform-infra output) |
|-------------|-----------------------------------|
| `dev` | `company-idp-github-deploy-dev` ARN |
| `staging` | `company-idp-github-deploy-staging` ARN |
| `production` | `company-idp-github-deploy-production` ARN |

Reusable workflows: `{{idpRepo}}` @ `{{idpRef}}`.

## Dependabot (production only)

**Dev/staging repos do not include active Dependabot** — auto dependency PRs can break CI/deploy.

When ready for production maintenance:

```sh
cp .github/dependabot.production.yml.example .github/dependabot.yml
git add .github/dependabot.yml
git commit -m "chore: enable production dependency updates"
git push
```

Optional: enable **Dependabot alerts** in GitHub → Settings → Code security (alerts only, no auto PRs).

